{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Instructions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Submit your Draft Executive Summary.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Your draft should be properly formatted, have a completed intro/methods section, and at least seven findings statements.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Your findings statements should be written with \u8220"X\u8221" as a placeholder for variables and percentages you do not have yet. At this point in the class most people will need to use \u8220"X\u8221" as a placeholder in all of their findings statements.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Example}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Final finding statement:} 73% of students reported that their favorite exercise was typing. (n=89)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Draft executive summary finding statement:} X% of students reported that their favorite exercise was XX. (n=x)\par}
